  "notes": "Official NMU Elementary Education PK-3, 3-6 dual-endorsement curriculum (Board of Trustees approved June 2024): 75-credit major in four tiers + gen-ed + electives = 120 total. Tier 1 Exploratory Introduction (9), Tier 2 Content Development (26), Tier 3 Methods Development (28), Tier 4 Internship Demonstration (12). EDU 101 carries PERS. EDU 425 (Additional Band PK-3, 3 cr) and EDU 430 (Internship Grades 3-6, 9 cr) selected from the either/or internship options. The source document labels EDU 300 'Professional Seminar II' (EDU 200 is also labeled II and EDU 400 is IV); rendered here as Professional Seminar III. Apprenticeship (A) courses pair with their base courses. 3.0 GPA required in the major, no grade below B-. MTTC required for certification. Semester placement follows the tier order as a sample sequence.",
